  "description": "Golden wire-format fixtures for energy_device MessageEnvelope over the Powerwall local v1r endpoint. Request cases are the serialized envelopes a reference client sends for each energy method (DIN 1232100-00-E--TG000000000000, clock frozen at 1800000000); a method that sends two messages lists both, in order. The reply case is a TEGAPIGetBackupEventsResponse whose manual backup event has ControlEventSchedulingInfo.priority = 2^64 - 1, the priority a max-backup event is scheduled at; it must decode without loss, which is why TypeScript types the field as a decimal string. Consumed identically by the TypeScript and Python test suites: both decoders must reach payload_case and both encoders must re-encode to the same bytes. canonical_hex, where present, is the canonical proto3 re-encoding of hex: the reference client writes a default-valued scalar explicitly, which neither generated encoder preserves.",
